openh264-esp32 — community fork of Cisco's OpenH264
==================================================

This repository is a community fork of https://github.com/cisco/openh264.
It adds a small ESP32 / ESP-IDF port of the decoder (see README.md). The
OpenH264 source, and the changes in this fork, are licensed under the
2-clause BSD license (see LICENSE).

Not the Cisco binary
-------------------
Cisco compiles and distributes a precompiled OpenH264 module from
openh264.org and maintains a royalty arrangement with the AVC patent pool
for THAT module. Builds produced from this source are not that module and
are not covered by that arrangement.

Patents
-------
H.264 / MPEG-4 AVC is covered by patents administered by patent pools
(e.g. Via LA). The BSD license grants no patent rights. If you build,
use, or distribute software containing an H.264 decoder derived from this
source, you are responsible for determining whether a patent licence is
required for your product and territory and for obtaining it. The authors
of this fork provide no patent grant and no legal advice.

